Package: gmsvar
Type: Package
Title: Graphical Identification of Structural Vector Autoregressions
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(person("Marco", "Reale", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "marco.reale@canterbury.ac.nz"),
             person("Anna", "Lin", role = "aut"),
             person("Granville", "Tunnicliffe Wilson", role = "aut"),
             person("Chris", "Price", role = "aut"),
             person("Blair", "Robertson", role = "aut"))
Description: Starting from the data, selects the lag order of a vector autoregression by information criteria,
    recovers a directed acyclic graph for the contemporaneous structure by an extended-BIC search over orderings (over all
    orderings for small systems, local search for larger ones; parent sets by backward elimination), identifies the arrows common to the Markov equivalence class under the time
    ordering, and estimates the structural VAR. An optional first stage restricts the search to a sparse conditional
    independence graph of the window of current and lagged variables (partial-correlation tests or penalised screens),
    estimated or supplied by the user, to impose prior knowledge or save computation. Includes impulse responses, a bootstrap of edge stability, and tools for simulating sparse
    structural VARs and scoring estimated graphs.
URL: https://github.com/MarcoNZreal/gmsvar
